### Nomos - Required Creation Order
### Each step validates that the referenced entities exist.
### Skipping a step returns a clear error (404 or 400).

### ============================================================
### Step 1: Create IDP (must exist before linking apps or creating rules)
### ============================================================

POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/idp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "auth0",
  "issuer": "https://auth0.example.com"
}

### ============================================================
### Step 2: Create App
### ============================================================

POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/app
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "appId": "mobile-app-br"
}

### ============================================================
### Step 3: Register audience (requires Step 1 + Step 2)
### ============================================================

POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/app/mobile-app-br/idp/auth0
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "audience": "mobile-br-auth0-client",
  "idpName": "auth0",
  "label": "Mobile BR Production"
}

### ============================================================
### Step 4: Create Proxy
### ============================================================

POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/proxy
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "account-service",
  "defaultPolicy": "deny"
}

### ============================================================
### Step 5: Grant access (requires Step 2 + Step 3 + Step 4)
### ============================================================

POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/access
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "appId": "mobile-app-br",
  "proxyName": "account-service",
  "audience": "mobile-br-auth0-client",
  "idpName": "auth0"
}

### ============================================================
### Step 6: Create rules (requires Step 1 + Step 4)
### ============================================================

POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/rule
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "proxyName": "account-service",
  "idpName": "auth0",
  "pathPattern": "/{country}/accounts/{msisdn}/balance",
  "methods": ["GET"],
  "validations": [
    {
      "order": 1,
      "level": 1,
      "paramName": "country",
      "source": "path",
      "jwtJsonPath": "$.country",
      "validation": "equals"
    },
    {
      "order": 2,
      "level": 2,
      "paramName": "msisdn",
      "source": "path",
      "jwtJsonPath": "$.aL",
      "validation": "contains"
    }
  ]
}

### ============================================================
### Error cases - what happens if you skip steps
### ============================================================

### ERROR: Link app to non-existent IDP (skipped Step 1)
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/app/mobile-app-br/idp/fake-idp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "audience": "some-audience",
  "label": "This will fail"
}
### → 404 { "error": "IDP_NOT_FOUND", "message": "IDP 'fake-idp' does not exist" }

### ERROR: Grant access with unregistered audience (skipped Step 3)
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/access
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "appId": "mobile-app-br",
  "proxyName": "account-service",
  "audience": "unregistered-audience",
  "idpName": "auth0"
}
### → 400 { "error": "AUDIENCE_NOT_REGISTERED", "message": "Audience 'unregistered-audience' is not registered for app 'mobile-app-br'" }

### ERROR: Create rule for non-existent proxy (skipped Step 4)
POST http://localhost:8080/nomos/v1/api/admin/rule
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "proxyName": "fake-proxy",
  "idpName": "auth0",
  "pathPattern": "/test",
  "methods": ["GET"],
  "validations": [
    {
      "order": 1,
      "level": 1,
      "paramName": "test",
      "source": "path",
      "jwtJsonPath": "$.test",
      "validation": "equals"
    }
  ]
}
### → 404 { "error": "PROXY_NOT_FOUND", "message": "Proxy 'fake-proxy' does not exist" }
